// The client, the five libraries it links against and the Arrow reader
// beside it are one repository and seven modules. This workspace is
// what makes a clone build without them being published first, and it
// is also what CI uses, because a library built by the workflow in this
// repository is the one that has to be tested rather than whatever the
// proxy already has.
//
// A workspace in a dependency is ignored, so this changes nothing for
// anybody who has installed the client. It goes away when the libraries
// are tagged and the go.mod requirements can stand on their own.
//
// One thing it does not cover: go mod tidy reads a module on its own
// and never the workspace around it, so until the libraries are tagged
// it will try to fetch lib/<goos>-<goarch>@v0.0.0 from the proxy and
// fail. Nothing else does, including go build, go vet, go test and the
// race detector. scripts/release.sh is what ends it, by tagging the
// libraries and rewriting the requirements to name what it tagged.
//
// The replacements below are why building zuarrow works at all. Being
// in the use list is enough for a module nothing outside the workspace
// is resolved against, which is what the client is: with zu_static it
// imports no library module and the tools never walk the graph. zuarrow
// imports arrow-go, and placing an import from outside the workspace
// means computing the build list, and computing it means reading the
// go.mod of every requirement by version, v0.0.0 included. A use
// directive does not answer that read and a replacement does. They go
// out with the same release that rewrites the requirements.

go 1.26.6

use (
	.
	./lib/darwin-amd64
	./lib/darwin-arm64
	./lib/linux-amd64
	./lib/linux-arm64
	./lib/windows-amd64
	./zuarrow
)

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go/lib/darwin-amd64 v0.0.0 => ./lib/darwin-amd64

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go/lib/darwin-arm64 v0.0.0 => ./lib/darwin-arm64

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go/lib/linux-amd64 v0.0.0 => ./lib/linux-amd64

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go/lib/linux-arm64 v0.0.0 => ./lib/linux-arm64

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go/lib/windows-amd64 v0.0.0 => ./lib/windows-amd64

replace github.com/tamnd/zu-go v0.0.0 => .
